    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "tonic-diatonic-substitution-target",
      "narrative": "For maj7, Larsen prescribes selecting upper-structure arpeggios by shared tones rather than root movement: over Fmaj7, use Am7 (rooted on the 3rd) because 'Fmaj7 and Am7 have three notes in common.' The arpeggio-on-the-3rd is the primary substitution, yielding the richest overlap. Chapter 1, p. 14.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "jens-larsen:modern-jazz-guitar-concepts:harmonic-substitution-lattice"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "modern-jazz-guitar-concepts",
