    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "tonic-pentatonic-as-extended-arpeggio",
      "narrative": "For tonic maj7, Larsen prescribes playing the minor pentatonic from the 3rd (e.g., E Minor Pentatonic over Cmaj7), reframing the pentatonic notes as a Dm7add11 extended arpeggio to make the harmonic rationale explicit: 'D F G A C / 1 b3 11(or4) 5 b7.' Chapter 1, p. 18.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "jens-larsen:modern-jazz-guitar-concepts:harmonic-substitution-lattice"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "modern-jazz-guitar-concepts",
