    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "tonic-minor-pentatonic-device",
      "narrative": "For tonic major chords, Larsen prescribes: 'Playing the minor pentatonic scale from the 3rd is a great device to use over tonic major chords.' This yields a characteristic coloring via the major 7th, 9th, 3rd, 5th, and 6th/13th. Chapter 4, p. 57.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "jens-larsen:modern-jazz-guitar-concepts:harmonic-substitution-lattice"
