    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "ii-chord-arpeggio-from-5th",
      "narrative": "For min7 functioning as a II chord, Larsen prescribes arpeggios built from the 5th degree: 'Playing the arpeggio from the 5th degree of the minor seventh chord creates a nice sound over a II chord, but you could consider adding the 3rd of the Dm7 chord, since that note is not in the arpeggio. Adding the third helps to clearly define the sound of the underlying chord.' Chapter 2, p. 35.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "jens-larsen:modern-jazz-guitar-concepts:harmonic-substitution-lattice"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "modern-jazz-guitar-concepts",
